# local rank-probe streak state (regenerated each run)
state/

# Downloaded MCP registry publisher binary (19MB Mach-O) — a tool, not source.
# ★2026-09-04: this read `mcp-publisherpackage-lock.json` for five weeks. #107
# (2026-07-30) appended to the line instead of after it, welding the pattern to
# a filename and matching nothing — so `git add -A` staged the 18MB binary the
# line exists to keep out, and nothing said so. package-lock.json is TRACKED
# and was never meant to be ignored; it was only ever the text that landed on
# the wrong line. test/gitignore-patterns-bite.test.mjs now asserts these
# patterns actually match, because a rule that silently stops matching is
# indistinguishable from one that was never written.
mcp-publisher

# git worktrees created inside the repo root (detached bases, ~4MB each).
# Same hazard as the binary above: untracked, so `git add -A` stages the lot.
wt-base/

# generated by scripts/check-served-manifest.mjs for the CI issue body
served-manifest-report.md
